Zeile 0: 0.05-2.74  Why you should never hire your brother-in-law for a heist.
Zeile 1: 2.84-7.11  In 1983, six robbers raided a warehouse at Heathrow Airport.
Zeile 2: 7.21-9.44  An inside guard had copied the key for them.
Zeile 3: 9.54-12.76  They poured petrol on the staff and demanded the vault codes.
Zeile 4: 12.86-17.68  They came for cash, but found three tonnes of gold. Twenty-six million pounds!
Zeile 5: 17.78-21.26  Police soon suspected the guard. He named his brother-in-law.
Zeile 6: 21.36-24.70  Two got twenty-five years. Most of the gold was never found.
Zeile 7: 24.80-29.55  Some say if you bought gold jewelry in Britain after 1983, you may be wearing it.
Zeile 8: 29.65-31.52  Would you still wear it?
